From: Crunch41 <70764418+Crunch41@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Say how to stop the room in the room-open log line

Patch 002 replaces the stdin loop with a SIGINT/SIGTERM shutdown, so
"Close with Q+Enter..." is wrong in a container. 002 used to change
that line itself, but upstream (1cd2ecd562) now builds the announce
session right below it under ENABLE_WEB_SERVICE, and a change on the
line next to that conflicts. Keeping the line change in its own patch
lets 002 apply with a clean 3-way merge.
---
 src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp b/src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp
--- a/src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp
+++ b/src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp
@@ -314,7 +314,7 @@ void LaunchRoom(int argc, char** argv, bool called_by_option) {
             LOG_INFO(Network, "Failed to create room: ");
             std::exit(-1);
         }
-        LOG_INFO(Network, "Room is open. Close with Q+Enter...");
+        LOG_INFO(Network, "Room is open. Stop the process to close it cleanly.");
 #ifdef ENABLE_WEB_SERVICE
         auto announce_session = std::make_unique<Core::AnnounceMultiplayerSession>(
             &WebService::MakeRoomJsonBackend);
